notes.body:
OK, so it's *not* a filter, it's a *named field*, and it shows the most recent packet for every value of that field it sees.

I.e., "eth.src" is something that can be used to construct an aggregation view, but "eth.src == 01:02:03:04:05:06" isn't.

(Terminology:

* a "field" or "named field" is a packet field, specified by name;
* a "packet-matching expression" is an expression constructed from fields, functions that operate on fields, etc. that returns a Boolean value when applied to a packet, indicating whether the packet is matched by the expression or not;
* a "display filter" is a packet-matching expression that's used to show, in the packet list, only packets that are matched by the expression;
* a "read filter" is a packet-matching expression that's used to ignore, when reading a capture file, packets are not matched by the expression;
* a "coloring rule" is a combination of a foreground color, a background color, a packet-matching expression, and an "enabled" flag, causing, if enabled, packets that are matched by the expression to be colored, in the packet list, using the foreground and background colors in question.)

Here is the current proposal:
https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/23802

@stigbjorlykke could you give us feedback please?

